  qs: [
    { q: "What does the doctor in the company office suggest about the journey?", o: ["That it will make Marlow rich", "That the real changes happen inside a man", "That the climate is healthy", "That he should refuse the post"], a: 1, ex: "قاس الطبيب رأسه وعلّق بأن التغيّرات تقع عادة في الداخل." },
    { q: "What detail shows the emptiness of the company's work at the first station?", o: ["A new hospital being built", "A railway that leads nowhere and a cliff blasted for no purpose", "A school full of children", "A market selling fresh food"], a: 1, ex: "وصف سكة حديد لا تفضي إلى شيء وجرفًا يُنسف بلا غرض ظاهر." },
    { q: "What is ironic about Kurtz's seventeen page report?", o: ["Nobody ever read it", "It was written in a language nobody spoke", "Its noble language ends with a note recommending destruction", "It was copied from another writer"], a: 2, ex: "النثر النبيل يتناقض تناقضًا صارخًا مع الجملة الأخيرة التي يوصي فيها بمحو تلك الشعوب." },
    { q: "\"His crew behaved throughout with a restraint that astonished him.\" What does restraint mean?", o: ["holding oneself back from acting", "great physical speed", "loud complaining", "careless behaviour"], a: 0, ex: "restraint تعني ضبط النفس والامتناع عن الاندفاع رغم الجوع والظروف." },
    { q: "Why does Marlow lie to Kurtz's betrothed?", o: ["He has forgotten the real words", "He wants money from her family", "He judges that the truth is too dark for that room", "The Russian asked him to"], a: 2, ex: "أدرك أن الحقيقة أشدّ سوادًا مما تحتمله تلك الغرفة، فآثر أن يقول لها اسمها." },
    { q: "What is the central irony of the whole novel?", o: ["The river is shorter than it appears", "A mission of light and progress becomes the darkest thing in the story", "Marlow never reaches the inner station", "Kurtz turns out to be a fine administrator"], a: 1, ex: "الرواية تكشف أن مشروع «التنوير والتقدم» كان نفسه أشدّ ما في الحكاية ظلامًا." }
  ],
  moral: "قد يكون أخطر الظلام لا في الأدغال البعيدة، بل في النفس حين ترفع عنها الرقابة وتسمّي طمعها رسالة."
